# Chroma library, modern Earth: MATURE stage (ages about 40 to 65). Grid: earth-plan.md. Rules: library-spec.md.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Compile and check the whole batch: python3 build.py earth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: calls WU (cycle s1) / calls BRG (cycle s3)

== a younger colleague needs a mentor
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: WU
tone: joy
life: work
horizon: months
roles: colleague, mentor, friend
earth: a newcomer half your age, at work or at the place where you volunteer, is told to learn from you
times: Many workers in midlife, every few years (estimate)
gap: 2-5
scene: {colleague} is half {Ns} age, sharp and a little lost, and {N} has been asked to show them the ropes.
scene W: The place has always paired each newcomer with someone older. This year it is {Ns} turn, and {N} means to do it properly.
scene U: {colleague} asks a question nobody has asked {N} in twenty years, and {N} realises they no longer remember why it is done that way.
scene B: {colleague} is clever, ambitious and already liked upstairs. Whoever trains them will have a friend near the top one day.
scene R: {colleague} bounds in on the first morning, all nerves and big ideas, and {N} remembers being exactly like that.
scene G: {N} learned this work at this same bench from old {mentor}. Now the knowledge has to pass on again, or it will be lost.
- W | take them through every procedure in order, and sign off each step | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 75
- U | ask them to teach you the new tools they learned at university | door | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | act: ask the newcomer to teach them the new tools learned at university | chance: 75
- B | teach them well, and make sure the bosses know who trained them | v: power, achievement | chance: 75
- R | throw them straight onto the biggest job going, and back them when they stumble | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 73
- G | let them watch you work for a few weeks before saying a word | v: tradition | act: let the newcomer watch them work for a few weeks before saying a word | chance: 72
- W>U | enrol them on the proper course, and check their progress every month | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 75
- U>B | brief them on how the place really works: who decides, and who to impress | v: power, achievement | chance: 75
- B>R | pull strings to get them onto the exciting project they are itching for | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 80
- R>G | tell them straight about every mistake you made at their age | v: benevolence | chance: 85
- G>W | bring them along to the old crowd's Friday lunch, so they belong | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 85
works: {colleague} handles the first big job alone, and handles it well.
works: Months later, {colleague} still stops by {Ns} desk, now to bring news rather than questions.
fails: {colleague} makes a costly mistake, and someone asks who trained them.
fails: {colleague} leaves for somewhere else before the year is out.

== a warning from the doctor
tier: everyday
at: hospital
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: BRG
tone: trouble
life: body
horizon: months
roles: partner, friend, a doctor
earth: the blood test shows high blood pressure and rising sugar, and the doctor says change now or pay later
times: Most people in midlife, once or twice; nearly half of US adults have high blood pressure and more than 1 in 3 have prediabetes (CDC)
gap: 6-12
scene: The doctor turns the screen so {N} can see the numbers: blood pressure and blood sugar, both far too high for comfort.
scene W: The doctor hands {N} a printed plan: a pill each morning, less salt, a walk every day. {N} reads it twice in the car.
scene U: {N} goes home with the printout and starts looking up what each number means, and what moves it.
scene B: The warning comes just when {N} can least afford to look weak, and {N} has no intention of being the one who is ill.
scene R: {N} walks out of the surgery furious: at the doctor, at the body, at the cake in the office kitchen.
scene G: {Ns} father had the same numbers at the same age. Some part of {N} has always been waiting for this.
- W | take the pills every morning and keep every appointment | habit | v: conformity, security | chance: 72
- U | buy a blood pressure cuff and log the numbers twice a day | habit | v: security, self-direction | chance: 62
- B | leave it off the form when you renew your life insurance | v: security, power | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: insurance fraud; backfire: the claim is refused when it is needed | chance: 25
- R | take up dancing every Friday night, and never miss a week | habit | v: hedonism, security | body: light | self_control: + | chance: 65
- G | skip the pills and trust your body to put itself right | identity | v: tradition (accepting one's lot) | closed: approval: going against the doctor's orders; backfire: a scare that ends in hospital | chance: 20
- W>R | sign up with a group of friends for a charity bike ride, and train for it | v: stimulation, benevolence | body: heavy | chance: 62
- U>G | read up on how the body heals itself, and give it what it needs | v: security, self-direction | chance: 55
- B>W | hire a strict personal trainer and pay for the whole year up front | habit | binds | v: security, achievement | tags: pay:money-.05 | chance: 75
- R>U | try a new diet every week until you find the one that works | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 54
- G>B | work it off on long, hard walks in the hills, and let nobody see you weaken | v: power (face), security | body: heavy | chance: 58
works: Six months on, the numbers are back where the doctor wants them.
works: {N} climbs the stairs at work without stopping, and notices.
fails: The next test is worse than the first.
fails: {N} keeps it up for three weeks, and then the old habits creep back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: calls UB (cycle s2) / calls WRG (cycle s4)

== someone tries to push you out at work
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: mature
age: 45-65
calls: UB
tone: trouble
life: work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, rival
needs: career
earth: a new manager half your age reorganises the department, and your job is not on the new chart
times: Many workers over 45, once or twice; more than half of US workers over 50 leave a long-held job before they choose to (ProPublica and Urban Institute 2018)
gap: 6-12
scene: {boss} has a new chart for the department, and {Ns} name sits in a small box off to one side, connected to nothing.
scene W: {N} has given the firm twenty years of good work, and there are rules about how people like {N} may be treated.
scene U: Someone is moving the pieces, and {N} wants to know who, and why, before making a single move.
scene B: {rival} smiles at {N} a great deal these days. {N} knows that smile; {N} has used it.
scene R: {N} hears it in a corridor, from someone who will not meet {Ns} eye, and feels the blood rise.
scene G: Every workplace has its seasons. The old trees come down so the young ones get the light.
- W | ask the personnel office for the rules on restructuring, in writing | v: security, conformity | chance: 58
- U | get into the manager's emails to find out who drew the chart, and why | v: security, power | closed: law: unauthorised access; backfire: caught, and dismissed on the spot | tech: computer | chance: 45
- B | take on the one project the new manager cannot do without | v: power, achievement | chance: 55
- R | march into the manager's office and tell them what you think of the chart | v: self-direction | closed: approval: insubordination; backfire: a formal warning on file | chance: 35
- G | accept that your season here is ending, and start clearing your desk slowly | v: tradition (accepting one's lot) | chance: 40
- W>B | get the union rep to win the biggest exit package the rules allow | v: power, security | tags: win:money+.1 | chance: 75
- U>R | line up a job elsewhere in secret, then resign on your own terms | v: self-direction | chance: 50
- B>G | bargain for a part-time role that leaves you more time at home | v: security, benevolence | chance: 68
- R>W | stand up at the team meeting and name what is happening to everyone over fifty | v: universalism (justice) | chance: 49
- G>U | ask the old hands who survived the last shake-up how they did it | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 55
works: The chart is redrawn, and {Ns} name is back in a box with lines running to it.
works: {N} leaves on {Ns} own terms, with more than {N} expected.
fails: {N} is called into a small room with a box of tissues on the table.
fails: {N} keeps the job, but loses all the work that mattered.

== a party for twenty-five years in the job
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: mature
age: 45-65
calls: WRG
tone: joy
life: friends, work
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, boss, friend, partner
needs: career
earth: you open the door of the pub's back room and forty workmates, old and new, shout your name: twenty-five years in the job
times: Rare: perhaps 1 in 6 workers, once; median job tenure for US workers aged 55 to 64 is about ten years (BLS 2022)
once: yes
share: .17
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: The lights snap on in the back room and forty faces shout {Ns} name. {colleague} has kept the secret for months: twenty-five years in the job.
scene W: Someone has made a slideshow of {Ns} working years, and everyone {N} owes something to is in the room. A speech will be expected.
scene U: {N} scans the room, trying to work out how {colleague} tracked down people who left years ago, and who told whom.
scene B: Half the room are people {N} trained or worked beside, and some of them now run whole companies.
scene R: The music is already loud, a drink is already in {Ns} hand, and nobody is talking about work. {N} feels very much alive.
scene G: Old workmates stand beside {Ns} family, and {N} sees twenty-five years of a working life gathered in one room.
- W | thank every guest by name before the night is out | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 92
- U | pull out the speech you secretly wrote years ago in case this ever happened | identity | v: achievement | chance: 80
- B | spend the evening beside the former trainee who now runs a big company | door | v: power, achievement | chance: 88
- R | dance on a table until the landlord asks you to get down | v: hedonism, stimulation | body: light | act: dance on a table until the landlord asks them to get down | chance: 85
- G | slip outside with the workmate you started with, and sit on the wall saying little | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 92
- W>G | announce that this will be a yearly gathering, same place, same date | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 75
- U>W | set up a group chat for everyone in the room, so nobody loses touch again | v: benevolence | tech: phone | chance: 92
- B>U | get an hour of free advice from the pensions expert among the guests | v: security, self-direction | chance: 85
- R>B | tell your boss, a little drunk, that you deserve a raise | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- G>R | let the young ones drag you onto the dance floor, and stay there | v: hedonism, benevolence | body: light | chance: 90
works: The night runs on until the staff switch the big lights on.
works: Weeks later, people are still sending {N} photographs from the party.
fails: Someone {N} wronged long ago turns up, and the room goes quiet.
fails: {N} spends the next day ill and embarrassed, piecing the night together.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 3: calls BR (cycle s3) / calls WUG (cycle s1)

== a sudden urge to buy something big
tier: everyday
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: BR
tone: mixed
life: money, inner
horizon: week
roles: partner, friend, sibling
earth: a motorbike, a sailing boat, a sports car: the thing in the showroom window you keep stopping to look at
times: Many people in midlife, every several years: the motorbike, the boat, the car (estimate)
gap: 3-6
scene: A motorbike gleams in the showroom window on {Ns} way home, and this week {N} has stopped to look at it three times.
scene W: For thirty years {N} has saved carefully. There is money for once, and a quiet voice says it is meant for the family.
scene U: {N} has read every review of the bike and knows exactly what it costs to insure, per year and per weekend.
scene B: {N} has worked hard for everything there is. Now {N} wants something that shows it.
scene R: The salesman tosses {N} the keys. The engine turns over, and something in {Ns} chest turns over with it.
scene G: {N} rode one just like it at nineteen. It feels less like buying something new than coming back to something old.
- W | talk it over with the family first, and abide by what you agree | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 68
- U | hire one for a month first, to see whether you really want it | v: self-direction, security | chance: 82
- B | buy the most expensive model, and park it where the neighbours will see | identity | v: power (face), achievement | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 69
- R | buy it on the spot, on finance, and ride it home | binds | v: hedonism, stimulation | body: light | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 74
- G | let the urge pass, as urges do, and walk on by | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 80
- W>R | put aside a fixed sum each month until you can pay for it in cash | v: hedonism, security | chance: 65
- U>G | research and buy a small plot of woodland instead | binds | v: universalism (nature) | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 70
- B>W | haggle hard for the safest, most sensible car on the lot instead | v: security | tech: car | chance: 78
- R>U | buy an old wreck of one on impulse, and teach yourself to restore it | v: self-direction | chance: 48
- G>B | wait for the end of the season, when the dealers are desperate, and pounce | v: achievement, power (resources) | chance: 75
works: {N} has it at last, and it is everything {N} hoped.
works: A year later, {N} does not regret a penny of it.
fails: The thing sits in the garage, hardly used, while the payments go on.
fails: The receipt turns up at home, and the row lasts a week.

== a long-planned trip
tier: everyday
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: WUG
tone: joy
life: leisure
horizon: week
roles: partner, friend, grandparent
earth: three weeks in the country you have dreamed of for twenty years, the tickets finally booked
times: About half of people, once or twice in a life, most often after fifty (estimate)
gap: 8-15
share: .5
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: After twenty years of talk, the tickets are in {Ns} hand: three weeks, a long flight, and a map with a route drawn on it in pencil.
scene W: {N} has a folder: bookings, insurance, copies of every passport, and a printed plan for each day.
scene U: {N} has studied the language for a year, and keeps a notebook of places no guidebook mentions.
scene B: The trip cost a great deal, and {N} intends to get every bit of value out of it.
scene R: Twenty years of saying "one day". The day is here, and {N} did not sleep at all last night.
scene G: The village {Ns} grandparents left long ago lies on the route. {N} wants to stand where they stood.
- W | follow the plan day by day, and see everything on the list | v: security, conformity | chance: 77
- U | spend the rainy days in the museums and archives, learning the history | v: self-direction | chance: 90
- B | upgrade every seat and every room with points you have hoarded for years | v: hedonism, power | chance: 73
- R | tear up the plan on the second day and follow wherever the road goes | door | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 88
- G | spend a whole day in an old forest, just sitting and watching | v: universalism (nature) | chance: 93
- W>U | book the guided tour with the best scholar of the region | door | v: self-direction | chance: 72
- U>B | study the local markets, and come home with things worth far more than their price | v: achievement, power | tags: win:money+.05 | chance: 40
- B>R | bribe your way onto the sold-out boat to the islands | v: stimulation | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: bribery; backfire: turned away at the pier and fined | chance: 70
- R>G | climb the mountain in the dark to watch the sun rise over the valley | v: stimulation, universalism (nature) | body: heavy | chance: 78
- G>W | find your distant cousins in the old village, and invite them all to dinner | door | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: made a friend | chance: 50
works: {N} comes home tired, sunburnt and changed in some way that is hard to name.
works: Years later, {N} still tells the story of the trip at every dinner.
fails: A lost bag and a fever eat the best week of the trip.
fails: The weather closes in, and the high road {N} came all this way for is shut.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 4: calls RG (cycle s4) / calls WUB (cycle s2)

== dancing at a wedding
tier: everyday
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: RG
tone: joy
life: leisure, family
horizon: moment
roles: sibling, partner, child, grandparent
earth: your niece's wedding: a band, an open bar, and three generations on the dance floor
times: Most people in midlife, a family wedding every few years (estimate)
gap: 2-4
scene: {Ns} niece is married, the band has started, and the dance floor is filling with aunts, uncles and small children.
scene W: The bride's family has planned every minute of the day, and the first dance is set for nine o'clock sharp.
scene U: {N} watches the dancers and notices that every family dances differently: who leads, who follows, who hangs back.
scene B: The groom's father is a man worth knowing, and he is standing alone by the bar.
scene R: The band strikes up a song {N} last danced to at twenty, and {Ns} feet start moving before {N} has decided anything.
scene G: {N} danced to this same old tune at {Ns} parents' anniversary. Now the young ones are dancing to it too.
- W | dance with each of the older relatives in turn, so nobody sits alone | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 92
- U | watch the steps for three songs, then join in and get them right | v: achievement | chance: 78
- B | make sure you get a dance with the groom's well-connected father | v: power | chance: 88
- R | dance until the band packs up, then sing all the way to the car park | v: hedonism | body: heavy | chance: 90
- G | kick off your shoes and dance the old dances with the grandmothers | v: tradition, hedonism | body: light | chance: 92
- W>G | get the whole family into the circle dance your people always do | identity | v: tradition | chance: 75
- U>W | fix the failing sound system so the party can go on | v: benevolence | chance: 55
- B>U | buy the old aunt drinks until she tells you the family secrets | v: power | act: buy the old aunt drinks until she tells them the family secrets | chance: 70
- R>B | dance a showy solo that has the whole room watching | v: power (face), hedonism | chance: 81
- G>R | slip outside with the young cousins and dance barefoot on the hotel's private lawn | v: hedonism, stimulation | body: light | closed: approval: the hotel's rules; backfire: asked to leave by the manager | chance: 82
works: The photographs the next day show {N} in the middle of every one.
works: {N} falls asleep in the car on the way home, still smiling.
fails: {N} twists a knee on the dance floor and limps for a month.
fails: A careless word at the bar starts a family quarrel that outlasts the wedding.

== your pension statement arrives
tier: everyday
stages: mature
age: 40-65
calls: WUB
tone: mixed
life: money
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, a financial adviser
earth: the yearly letter says you will retire on about half of what you live on now
times: Most workers with a pension, once a year when the statement comes (estimate)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: The yearly pension letter is on the mat. {N} reads the line near the bottom twice: about half of what {N} lives on now.
scene W: {N} has paid in every month for twenty-five years, exactly as advised. The letter says it is not enough.
scene U: {N} spreads the statements across the table with a calculator and a pot of coffee. Somewhere in here is a better plan.
scene B: {N} reads the figure and starts counting what can be sold, cut, moved or squeezed to change it.
scene R: {N} reads the letter, laughs, and wonders aloud who knows whether {N} will even live that long.
scene G: {Ns} parents retired on very little and lived well enough, with a garden and each other.
- W | raise your payments to the level the adviser recommends, and leave it alone | v: security, conformity | chance: 78
- U | build a spreadsheet of every year from now to ninety | v: security, self-direction | tech: computer | chance: 75
- B | move everything into the riskiest fund with the best returns | v: power, achievement | mark: took a wild risk | tags: win:money+.15; lose:money-.15 | chance: 60
- R | drop the letter in the bin and book a holiday | v: hedonism | tags: pay:money-.05 | chance: 30
- G | plan to grow more of your own food and need less | habit | v: security, tradition | chance: 45
- W>B | trace and claim, by the book, every old pension from every past job | v: security, power (resources) | chance: 68
- U>R | work out exactly how many years you need, then plan your early escape | v: self-direction | chance: 65
- B>G | buy a cheap, run-down cottage near family to retire into | binds | v: security, benevolence | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 65
- R>W | rage at the letter, then set yourself a strict budget and keep to it | v: security, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the family's old folk how they managed on so little, and write it down | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 72
works: The new plan adds up, and {N} sleeps better for it.
works: By the next statement, the line at the bottom has moved the right way.
fails: The fund {N} chose falls by a fifth in one bad month.
fails: {N} means to sort it out, and the letter sits in a drawer for another year.

