== the club or congregation asks you to lead
tier: everyday
stages: mature
age: 40-70
calls: WG
tone: mixed
life: community, faith
horizon: years
roles: elder, friend, rival, grandparent
rite: mature
earth: the choir, the rowing club or the congregation needs a new chair, and everyone looks at you
times: About 1 in 4 people in midlife, once or twice; about 1 in 4 US adults volunteer through a group (AmeriCorps 2021)
gap: 6-12
share: .25
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: The old chair is stepping down after eighteen years, and at the end of the meeting three people in a row ask {N} to stand.
scene W: The circle has kept going for a century because someone always said yes when asked. This year they are asking {N}.
scene U: {N} has seen the accounts, the minutes and the falling numbers, and already has ideas about what is wrong.
scene B: Whoever takes the chair sets the agenda, signs the cheques and hears everyone's business first.
scene R: {N} is tired of watching the same few people make the same old mistakes. Maybe it is time to shake things up.
scene G: {Ns} grandmother once chaired this same circle, and her photograph still hangs in the hall.
- W | accept, and take on the duties from the next meeting | v: benevolence, conformity | tags: commit:community | chance: 69
- U | ask to see the books first, and stand only if you can fix them | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 72
- B | stand, and fill the committee with your own allies | v: power | mark: made an enemy | tags: commit:community | chance: 55
- R | tell them honestly you are no longer sure you believe in what it stands for | identity | v: self-direction | chance: 50
- G | leave it to the oldest members to say whether you are ready | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 65
- W>U | accept, and set up proper training for every volunteer | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 65
- U>B | study the rules until you know exactly how to win the vote | v: power | chance: 65
- B>R | take the chair, then use it to scrap the dull old rules | v: self-direction, power | chance: 49
- R>G | speak from the heart about what this place has meant to your family | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 80
- G>W | say yes, because your grandmother would have | binds | v: tradition, benevolence | tags: commit:community | chance: 75
works: Within a year the hall is fuller than it has been in a long time.
works: The first year ends with the books balanced and nobody resigning in a huff.
fails: {N} spends the year in meetings that go nowhere.
fails: A faction forms against {N}, and some old friendships cool for good.

